\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 DHL\uc2  Workers Walk Out At Kentucky Cargo Hub\b0\par\par\uc2 By J. Edward Moreno \par \uc2 525 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2023\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 6\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers who load and unload cargo planes at \uc2 DHL\uc2 's hub near Cincinnati walked out after months of negotiations failed to produce a contract.\par \par \uc2 More than 1,100 workers at \uc2 DHL Express\uc2 's global air cargo hub at Cincinnati/Northern Kentucky International Airport went on strike on Thursday after months of failed negotiations with the parcel carrier.\par \par \uc2 A group of \uc2 DHL\uc2  workers at the hub who load and unload planes voted in April to unionize with the \uc2 International Brotherhood of Teamsters\uc2 , which has been in contract negotiations with the company since July. The union has filed more than 20 unfair labor practice complaints with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  since then, accusing the company of retaliation against organized workers. \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  Local 100, which represents the unionized workers, voted to authorize a strike on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 ''The company forced this work stoppage, but \uc2 DHL\uc2  has the opportunity to right this wrong by respecting our members and coming to terms on a strong contract,'' Bill Davis, president of Local 100, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 DHL Express\uc2  is the U.S. unit of the world's largest logistics company, \uc2 Deutsche Post\uc2 , but accounts for only 2.3 percent of the market in the United States in package volume, according to the Pitney Bowes Parcel Shipping Index. As a German company, it is not able to ship between domestic airports within the United States, so it has to contract out those services and instead focuses on handling international shipments.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 DHL\uc2  spokesman said the company ''was fully prepared for this anticipated tactic and has enacted contingency plans'' like redirecting shipments to avoid Cincinnati and adding replacement staff members.\par \par \uc2 The company noted that roughly 4,000 employees at the facility were still on the job. It said it did not ''anticipate any significant disruptions to our service performance.''\par \par \uc2 ''Unfortunately, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  decided to try and influence these negotiations and pressure the company to agree to unreasonable contract terms by taking a job action,'' the company spokesman said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 DHL\uc2  strike comes at a time of increased tensions in the industry between companies and organized labor.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  threated to strike at a \uc2 United Parcel Service\uc2  facility in Louisville, Ky., accusing the company of engaging in ''similar practices to disrespect and abuse our members in the same state'' by laying off administrative workers who had just voted to unionize. The union threatened to strike at UPS as well if it ''doesn't get its act together'' by Monday.\par \par \uc2 UPS narrowly averted a strike over the summer after contentious negotiations with the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 , which threatened to halt operations for the country's largest parcel service.\par \par \uc2 The facility where \uc2 DHL\uc2  workers are striking is directly in front of Amazon's Air Hub, where a unionization effort is underway. Workers there have accused Amazon of illegally impeding organizing efforts.\par \par \uc2 Union members at DHL protesting at the Cincinnati/Northern Kentucky International Airport near the DHL Express Hub on Friday in Erlanger, Ky. (PHOTOGRAPH BY CAROLYN KASTER/ASSOCIATED PRESS) This article appeared in print on page B6. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020231209ejc90003e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
