\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Santul Nerkar and Brooks Barnes \par \uc2 563 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 November 2023\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 Job Openings Remained Steady in September\par \par \uc2 Job openings changed little in September, the Labor Department announced on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 There were 9.6 million job openings in September, slightly up from August's revised total of 9.5 million, according to seasonally adjusted figures from the Job Openings and Labor Turnover Survey. The figure was greater than economists' expectations of 9.3 million openings. The rate of workers quitting their jobs was flat, at 2.3 percent, for the third straight month.\par \par \uc2 Job openings, which reached a record of more than 12 million in March 2022, have trended down, as has the job-quitting rate, while separations have been flat.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  closely monitors job openings to understand whether the economy is running too hot. Since March 2022, the Fed has tried to fight inflation by raising interest rates to their highest level since 2001.\par \par \uc2 Less churn in the labor market indicates that interest rate increases are having an effect, said \uc2 Julia Pollak\uc2 , the chief economist at the job search website \uc2 ZipRecruiter\uc2 . \uc2 ZipRecruiter\uc2 's latest survey of new employees found that the share of hires who received a pay increase, got a signing bonus or were recruited to their new jobs each fell.\par \par \uc2 Job openings remain much higher than they were before the pandemic, and the number of unemployed workers per job opening is much lower. Both are signs of a tight labor market. SANTUL NERKAR\par \par \uc2 STREAMING SERVICES\par \par \uc2 Disney\uc2  Seizing Option to Take Control of \uc2 Hulu\par \par \uc2 The tug of war over \uc2 Hulu\uc2  is over.\par \par \uc2 The Walt Disney Company\uc2  said on Wednesday that it would take full control of \uc2 Hulu\uc2 , one of the world's most popular streaming services, by paying at least $8.61 billion to buy out \uc2 Comcast\uc2 , which owned a 33 percent stake. \uc2 Comcast\uc2  triggered the deal as part of a ''put-call'' agreement between the companies in 2019. The ultimate price will be determined by an appraisal process that will drag into next year.\par \par \uc2 Comcast\uc2 , which recently stopped supplying \uc2 Hulu\uc2  with shows like ''Saturday Night Live'' and ''The Voice,'' rerouting them instead to its Peacock streaming service, said in September that it had sped up negotiations to sell \uc2 Hulu\uc2  to \uc2 Disney\uc2 . Previously, \uc2 Comcast\uc2  and \uc2 Disney\uc2  agreed that \uc2 Comcast\uc2  could force \uc2 Disney\uc2  to buy its stake early next year (the ''put''). At the same time, \uc2 Disney\uc2  had the ability at that point to require \uc2 Comcast\uc2  to sell (the ''call'').\par \par \uc2 ''The acquisition of \uc2 Comcast\uc2 's stake in \uc2 Hulu\uc2  at fair market value will further \uc2 Disney\uc2 's streaming objectives,'' \uc2 Disney\uc2  said in a statement. \uc2 Hulu\uc2 , which has roughly 48 million subscribers, offers programming from ABC, FX, Fox and other traditional networks, along with original shows like ''Only Murders in the Building'' and ''The Kardashians.''\par \par \uc2 As part of its push to make its flagship \uc2 Disney\uc2 + streaming service profitable, \uc2 Disney\uc2  announced this year that content from \uc2 Hulu\uc2  would be made available on \uc2 Disney\uc2 + to subscribers of both services in the United States. (\uc2 Hulu\uc2  does not operate overseas.) \uc2 Disney\uc2  plans to roll out this ''one app experience'' by the end of the year. \uc2 Hulu\uc2  will also continue as a stand-alone product, charging $18 for ad-free access and $8 for an ad-supported option. BROOKS BARNES\par \par \uc2 (PHOTOGRAPH BY NATI HARNIK/ASSOCIATED PRESS) This article appeared in print on page B2. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020231102ejb20004i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
