\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By The Associated Press and Reuters \par \uc2 514 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 September 2023\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WORK FORCE\par \par \uc2 California Law Increases Pay of Fast-Food Workers\par \par \uc2 California fast food workers will be paid at least $20 per hour next year under a new law signed Thursday by Gov. \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 . When it takes effect on April 1, fast food workers in California will have among the highest minimum wages in the country, according to data compiled by the University of California-Berkeley Center for Labor Research and Education. The state's minimum wage for all other workers, $15.50, is already among the nation's highest. The law settles a fight between labor and business groups over how to regulate the industry. In exchange for higher pay, labor unions have dropped their attempt to make fast food corporations liable for the misdeeds of their independent franchise operators in California, an action that could have upended the business model on which the industry is based. The industry, meanwhile, has agreed to pull a referendum related to worker wages off the 2024 ballot. ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 AIRLINES\par \par \uc2 United To Improve Travel For Wheelchair Customers\par \par \uc2 United Airlines\uc2  has agreed to improve air travel for passengers in wheelchairs after the federal government investigated a complaint by a disability-rights advocate. United and the Transportation Department said Thursday that the airline would add a filter to the booking tool on its website to help consumers find flights on which the plane can more easily accommodate their wheelchairs. The cargo doors on some planes are too small to easily get a motorized wheelchair into the plane. United said it expects to make the changes by early next year. The settlement followed a complaint filed by Engracia Figueroa, who said her custom-made wheelchair was damaged on a United flight in 2021. She died three months later, and family members and her lawyer blamed sores, skin grafts and emergency surgery on sitting for five hours in a manual wheelchair that did not fit her body. ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 GAMING\par \par \uc2 GameStop\uc2 's New Chief to Lead Turnaround Push\par \par \uc2 GameStop\uc2  named the activist investor \uc2 Ryan Cohen\uc2  as its chief executive and chairman on Thursday, tightening his grip on the ailing videogame retailer that he intends to turn around. The brick-and-mortar retailer that once attracted gamers has struggled in the age of online downloads, drawing it to the heart of a clash in 2021 between hedge funds betting on its demise and retail traders pumping up its price. At the peak of that meme stock rally, Mr. Cohen, \uc2 GameStop\uc2 's largest investor, joined the board to aid a pivot to e-commerce. His shot to fame was building up an online pet products retailer \uc2 Chewy\uc2  into a powerhouse that he sold for $3.5 billion in 2017. Mr. Cohen became executive chairman at \uc2 Gamestop\uc2  in June after the former chief, \uc2 Matt Furlong\uc2 , was ousted. The company said he will relinquish that title and will not receive any compensation for his new roles. REUTERS\par \par \uc2 (PHOTOGRAPH BY DAVID J. PHILLIP/ASSOCIATED PRESS) This article appeared in print on page B2. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020230929ej9t0004y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
